<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- App Sandbox: required for a provisioning-signed macOS app. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
  <true/>

  <!--
    keychain-access-groups — the RESTRICTED entitlement this probe needs.

    Why it must be (and here is) adaptive:
    A Secure Enclave key lives in the keychain and is scoped to an "access
    group". macOS only hands out the key to a process whose code signature
    carries a keychain-access-groups entitlement AND that entitlement is backed
    by a provisioning profile (i.e. a real Xcode build). The group is normally
    "<TeamID>.<bundle-id>", so instead of hardcoding a team we use the build
    variables: $(AppIdentifierPrefix) == <TeamID>. and $(CFBundleIdentifier) ==
    the app's bundle id. This resolves to the correct group for EVERY developer
    automatically, so no per-dev editing is needed.

    ⚠️ This entitlement is "restricted": it can NOT be added by hand-code-signing
    a bare binary (macOS rejects the app: RBS Code 5 / SIGKILL 137). It is only
    honored on builds signed through Xcode + a provisioning profile — which is
    exactly what Automatic signing + "pick your Team" produces.
  -->
  <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
  <array>
    <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)$(CFBundleIdentifier)</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
